30,2,,status,Benjamin,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":1,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
31,2,,status,Kenji,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":2,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
32,2,,status,Toshio,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":3,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
33,2,,status,Daisuke,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":4,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
34,2,,status,Rin,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
35,2,1,talk,Daisuke,,"Um... the results are a bit worrying. The suspended bay has a weight limit of four hundred kilos per square metre, and the powered displays had seventeen call-outs last season. Some areas even had to be roped off.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Toshio,,The data suggests a clear pattern. Visitors are drawn to movement and human presence; static displays of cased objects result in lower attendance and fewer repeat visits. We must prioritize engagement over mere preservation.,"{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Rin,,Oh no! The conservation lab is in big trouble! There's only one person working there and a huge pile of things waiting to be fixed. We can't pick something that needs too much cleaning!,"{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Kenji,,"Wow, you guys found some big problems! I found out that shipping is super expensive—almost a third of installation costs! Plus, two of the last four shows had delays because of paperwork. We can't let that happen again!","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Benjamin,,"It seems we are plagued by a series of expensive inefficiencies. I've discovered that bespoke mount-making costs are escalating, and our evening hires are occasionally leaving us with damaged displays. It appears the budget is leaking from several corners.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Daisuke,,"I... I'm really concerned. If we pick something too heavy or with too many electronics, we might actually damage the gallery or have to close parts of it again. We have to be very careful.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Toshio,,"@Daisuke, caution is necessary, but we cannot let fear lead to a sterile exhibition. If we avoid all risk, we risk a show that no one visits. We need a balance of safety and dynamism.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Rin,,"@Toshio, but it's not just about being scared! If we pick a huge show and the one person in the lab has to do everything, they'll just collapse! We need a plan that doesn't break the people!","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Kenji,,"@Rin, you're totally right! We can't break the people or the budget. And @Daisuke, if we pick something with too many overseas loans, we might have the same paperwork mess and delays as before!","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Rin"",""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Benjamin,,"It is a fascinating tapestry of dysfunction we've woven, is it not? Between the crumbling electronics, the exhausted staff, and the escalating costs of custom mounts, we are essentially planning a miracle. We must seek a candidate that is remarkably self-sufficient.","{""words"":41,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Daisuke,,"I... I agree with @Benjamin. A self-sufficient exhibition sounds safest. If we choose something lightweight and simple, we won't risk the floor or the power systems, and maybe the lab won't be so overwhelmed.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Toshio,,"Simplicity for the sake of safety is a trap, @Daisuke. If we prioritize a ""safe"" choice that lacks engagement, we are merely ensuring a failure of a different kind: a gallery that remains empty.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Rin,,"@Toshio, but an empty gallery is better than a broken one! If the lab person gets sick because they're too tired, who will fix the things? We have to be nice to the people who work here!","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Kenji,,"@Rin, exactly! And @Toshio, we can still make it exciting without it being a disaster! If we pick something that doesn't rely on a million overseas shipments, we won't have to apologize to visitors for missing art!","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Rin"",""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Benjamin,,"@Toshio, while I admire your commitment to dynamism, we must acknowledge that ""engagement"" is a costly luxury when our infrastructure is fraying. A show that arrives with its own supports would be a blessing.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Daisuke,,"I... I just don't want anything to break. If we can find a candidate that is light and doesn't need much power, I think that would be the most responsible choice for the museum.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Toshio,,"Responsibility also means ensuring the museum fulfills its purpose. If we choose a candidate solely to avoid risk, we ignore the visitors' desire for interaction. We must find a way to integrate human presence and movement safely.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Rin,,"@Toshio, we can have human presence with the volunteers! But we can't just ignore the lab. If we pick a show that's too hard to set up, the staff will be too tired to be friendly!","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Kenji,,"I agree! Let's look for a candidate that's easy on the staff and doesn't have a scary amount of overseas shipping. That way, everything arrives on time and everyone stays happy! I'm ready to see the options!","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Benjamin,,It appears we have reached a consensus on the necessity of pragmatism. Let us hope the candidates offer us a solution that is as fiscally discreet as it is structurally sound. I am ready to review the options.,"{""words"":38,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
55,3,,status,Benjamin,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":1,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
56,3,,status,Kenji,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":2,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
