59,3,,status,Rin,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
60,3,1,talk,Daisuke,,"Um... I think Option A is the safest. It's local, so it's not heavy on shipping, and textiles are light. It doesn't seem to need much power or heavy rigging, which would protect the floor.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Toshio,,Option A is strong because it includes demonstration sessions. My research shows that human presence and activity are what drive repeat visits. It balances @Daisuke's need for safety with the public's desire for engagement.,"{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,Rin,,"I like Option A too! It's local, so the lab person won't have to clean a million things from far away, and the craftspeople can help out so the staff doesn't get too tired!","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Kenji,,"Option A is awesome! Since it's local, we won't have to worry about those scary shipping delays or expensive transport costs. Everything will actually be here on time! I vote for Option A!","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Benjamin,,"Option A is remarkably prudent. Local sourcing minimizes transport costs, and the inclusion of demonstration sessions provides the dynamism @Toshio desires without the fiscal volatility of bespoke mounts or complex rigging. It is a most elegant solution.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Daisuke,,I... I feel much better now that we all agree. Option A seems to respect the building's limits and the staff's well-being. I'm happy to vote for it.,"{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Toshio,,It is rare that our disparate concerns align so perfectly. Option A satisfies the structural and logistical constraints while ensuring the exhibition remains a living experience rather than a static display. I am satisfied.,"{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Rin,,"Me too! It's the kindest choice for everyone. The lab person can breathe, the volunteers can help, and the visitors get to see real people working. I'm voting for Option A!","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Kenji,,"@Rin, you're so right! It's a win-win for everyone. No shipping nightmares, no stressed-out staff, and a cool show for the visitors. I'm definitely sticking with Option A!","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Benjamin,,It is a rare pleasure when the path of least resistance also happens to be the most logical. Option A avoids the budget-swallowing pitfalls of international logistics and custom installations. I shall join the chorus.,"{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Daisuke,,I... I'm glad we could find something that makes everyone feel comfortable. I'll vote for Option A. It's the most responsible way to protect the gallery and the people.,"{""words"":29,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Toshio,,"The evidence is conclusive. Option A provides the human interaction and activity that the public craves, without compromising the museum's fragile infrastructure. It is the only choice that ensures both stability and success. I vote for Option A.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,Rin,,I'm so happy we all agree! Option A is the best because it's friendly to the staff and the building. I'm voting for Option A!,"{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Kenji,,I'm so glad we're all on the same page! Option A is the way to go. No more apologies at the door for us! I'm voting for Option A!,"{""words"":29,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Benjamin,,"Indeed, the alignment is quite seamless. Option A is a masterclass in risk mitigation, ensuring our budget remains intact and our staff sane. I shall cast my vote for Option A with a clear conscience.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,4,talk,Daisuke,,I... I'm really relieved. Thank you everyone for listening to my worries. I'll cast my vote for Option A. It's the safest and kindest choice for the museum.,"{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,4,talk,Toshio,,"The data and the options have led us to a singular, logical conclusion. Option A is the only candidate that secures both the museum's integrity and the visitors' interest. I vote for Option A.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,4,talk,Rin,,Yay! I'm so glad we're all being so nice to the staff! Option A is definitely the winner because it's the happiest choice for everyone. I vote for Option A!,"{""words"":30,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,4,talk,Kenji,,"This is going to be the best exhibition ever! Everyone is happy, the budget is safe, and the art will actually be here! I'm super excited! I vote for Option A!","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,4,talk,Benjamin,,A most harmonious conclusion. We have successfully navigated the treacherous waters of our museum's inefficiencies to find a sanctuary of stability. I cast my vote for Option A.,"{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
